meta {
  name: Delete video
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Deletes a video and everything it owns: the raw upload, every HLS playlist and segment, the thumbnail, any open multipart upload and any queued transcode job. Storage goes first and the row last, so a failure part-way can simply be retried.

  Who: a club admin, or the uploader while they are still club_owner or admin. Same rule as editing.

  | Status | Code | When |
  |---|---|---|
  | 204 | | deleted |
  | 403 | `FORBIDDEN` | you can see the video but not manage it |
  | 404 | `VIDEO_NOT_FOUND` | you can't see it, or it was already deleted |
  | 409 | `VIDEO_PROCESSING` | a worker is transcoding it right now; retry when it finishes |

  A video that is still `UPLOADING` can be deleted: the multipart upload is aborted first, and any part the client sends afterwards is refused by storage.

  Example 409:

  ```json
  {
    "error": {
      "code": "VIDEO_PROCESSING",
      "message": "This video is being processed. Try again when processing finishes."
    },
    "requestId": "c60b3960-517e-4b49-8d08-9b0309bfc1a4"
  }
  ```
}
